<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_ScariaOnsetArming.xml            UtinniPatches - SCARLANDS_MECHANICS_2 build pass

  scarlands_kit_spec.md §3. Reuses ruled comp RC5's GameCondition_
  ArmLatentHazard, extended this spike pass with pawnKindFilter/
  requiredHediff (both BUILT, compiling, 0 warnings/errors) specifically for
  this mechanic: arm ONLY the plated grazers that already rolled vanilla
  Scaria (biome's own wildAnimalScariaChance, see RUT_Scarlands.xml) — never
  every animal on the map, never a grazer that never carried the disease at
  all.

  pawnKindFilter: the two PawnKindDefs RUT_Scarlands.xml's own wildAnimals
  list already comments "plated-grazer, keep" — RSW_FoundryBeetle (our own
  clone, mandrake.rsw.swbestiary) and AA_SpinedGow (Alpha Animals,
  sarg.alphaanimals, already referenced elsewhere in the campaign, e.g.
  BiomeCast_Ashkarr.xml). AA_Helixien is commented "mortuary-guild,
  adjust-keep" on that same list — NOT a plated grazer, deliberately
  excluded here.

  requiredHediff: vanilla Scaria (HediffDefOf.Scaria, defName "Scaria",
  RimSage-confirmed) — a pawn must already carry it, so this sweep only ever
  touches animals the biome's own roll already marked.

  chancePerPawn left at its 1.0 default: the biome's own
  wildAnimalScariaChance (0.5) is the only dice roll in this mechanic — "the
  wildlife carries the madness; the plated grazers always succumb in the
  end" (the_scarlands.md, quoted in the kit spec) reads as 100% eventual
  onset for every animal that already has Scaria, not a second, independent
  chance layered on top.

  intervalTicks 60000 (1 game day) and armImmediately=true are this build
  pass's own INVENTED-BUILD sweep cadence — the spec gives no number for how
  often the sweep itself runs (only for the incubation hediff's own climb
  rate, on RUT_ScariaIncubation.xml), and armImmediately keeps a fresh
  colony from waiting out a full day before any grazer already on the map
  can be swept.

  🔴 BUG FOUND AND FIXED THIS PASS: RUT_Scarlands.xml (a fresh BiomeDef with
  no ParentName) never carried <wildAnimalScariaChance> at all — the donor
  vanilla Scarlands.xml sets 0.5, but our own biome def silently defaulted
  to BiomeDef's own field default of 0 (decompile-confirmed,
  RimWorld/BiomeDef.cs:101). Without that field this mechanic's own arming
  gate (requiredHediff=Scaria) would have nothing to ever find — zero wild
  animals would ever carry vanilla Scaria to begin with. Fixed in
  RUT_Scarlands.xml this same pass (see that file's own header note).

  MayRequire is load-bearing: conditionClass and the modExtension both live
  in mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards.
-->
<Defs>

  <GameConditionDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_ScariaOnsetArming</defName>
    <conditionClass>RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.GameCondition_ArmLatentHazard</conditionClass>
    <label>the madness inevitably comes</label>
    <description>The plated grazers graze on, placid as ever. It never lasts. Sooner or later, every one of them snaps.</description>
    <canBePermanent>true</canBePermanent>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.ArmLatentHazardExtension">
        <hediffToApply>RUT_ScariaIncubation</hediffToApply>
        <intervalTicks>60000</intervalTicks>
        <armImmediately>true</armImmediately>
        <targets>Animals</targets>
        <pawnKindFilter>
          <li MayRequire="mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">RSW_FoundryBeetle</li>
          <li MayRequire="sarg.alphaanimals">AA_SpinedGow</li>
        </pawnKindFilter>
        <requiredHediff>Scaria</requiredHediff>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </GameConditionDef>

</Defs>
